==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Gold Cat was a part of three other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Get Rich (Removed Combo)|Get Rich]], [[Biceps (Removed Combo)|Biceps]] and [[Precious Metals (Removed Combo)|Precious Metals]].
*Prior to [[Version 14.1 Update|Version 14.1]], [[Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Neneko]], Gold Cat, [[Cat Base Mini (Super Rare Cat)|Cat Base Mini]] and [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] could only be unlocked when "Limited Edition" was part of the current pool.
*Gold Cat and [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] are the only [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cats]] that can be exchanged for more than 478,000 XP.
*Though Gold Cat is a Super Rare unit, it has the same upgrade costs as Cat.
*Glittering Macho Cat is one of the units to have his description rewritten in [[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]], as "Immune to Wave attacks" was changed to "Immune to Waves".
*The Japanese names of this unit and [[Commander Cat (Special Cat)|Gold Nyanko Ranger]] both translate to "Gold Cat", but aren't the same. Gold Cat's is 金ネコ ''Kin Neko'', while Gold Nyanko Ranger's is ゴールドにゃんこ ''Gōrudo Nyanko''.
*One of the possible [[Cat Shrine#Cat Fortune|Cat Fortunes]] is "Time to cash in your Gold Cats!"

